    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0041" n="35" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg35"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865D.01/604: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-21T17:00:00-05:00">January 21, 1942—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>66. It is assumed that your 95, January 16, 5 p.m., is not intended as an answer
                    to the Department’s 9, January 3, 10 p.m.,<anchor n="14" xml:id="d42-f1"/> and
                    that the information requested in the latter message concerning law and justice
                    in Eritrea will be forthcoming as soon as possible.</p>
                <pb facs="0042" n="36" xml:id="pg36"/>
                <p>The Department does not appear to have received the terms of Eden’s pledge to the
                    Senussi with respect to Cirenaica, and would be glad to receive them together
                    with your comments regarding the compatibility of the pledge with any
                    arrangement which may be contemplated with Egypt relating to the future
                    disposition of Cirenaica.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
